From bf1e540e2c230d612daa738fa08f0ccebbadcce2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 06:08:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(strategy): six funnels the pages actually render, a
 citable framework endpoint, and an expansion order that names what it does
 not know
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Four registries, one rule: nothing here may assert something the repository
cannot back, and a build guard enforces it.

FUNNELS — every page on this site ended the same way: book a free measure.
That is correct for exactly one of the six reasons somebody arrives. A
homeowner halfway through comparing three quotes is not refusing to book; they
have not decided, and a booking button at that moment reads as not having
listened. lib/funnels declares six intents, the tool that serves each, the
event that completes it, and — the field that does the real work — what its
visitor is NOT ready for, so the next edit does not put an estimate button at
the top of a diagnostic page. <NextStep> renders the matched call on twelve
routes and nothing at all on a route that carries no intent.

/api/v1/framework — the Well-Installed Framework as versioned, citable data:
every criterion, its risk, its severity, and the paper section behind it, CC BY
and unauthenticated. It publishes what the framework refuses to do, which is
the part a competitor's marketing page cannot copy.

EXPANSION ORDER — every Ontario market ranked out of 100 from four things this
repository can source: routing, adjacency, a confirmed position on a date, and
published evidence. It carries the ten economic inputs it does NOT hold, named
in the payload of /api/v1/markets rather than estimated, because a ranking that
quietly includes a population figure nobody sourced directs capital on a number
somebody typed. 27 of 43 Ontario markets score zero on confirmation — not
because the work is not done there, but because nobody has written the sentence
and the date. That is the bottleneck, and it is not a software problem.

TRACKED QUESTIONS — 33 questions across five families, each mapped to the page
that answers it or declared as a gap (two are). scripts/aeo-score.mjs turns a
month of human observations into a score, a trend, and the list of questions
this site answers and is cited for by nobody. It deliberately does not query
the answer engines: automating them is governed by their terms, and a scraped
number would be precise and dishonest.

verify:strategy — seven checks, each with a regression: tool and next-step
routes resolve; a completion event is actually emitted somewhere and not merely
declared in the union; every funnel names its notYet; tracked coverage resolves
(this caught /glossary/gapping, which does not exist — the slug is
seasonal-gapping); ids are unique; the scorecard still refuses the ten economic
inputs; and every route in ROUTE_FUNNEL renders <NextStep>, so a funnel cannot
live only in lib/ where no visitor sees it.

63 guards green, 291 tests, tsc at its 115-error baseline with nothing new.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
